# ── Derived data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under data/ is reproducible: calibrated/ (uncal/rate pools) re-downloads from
# MAST, stage1/ stage2/ mosaics/ regenerate from scripts/reduce_nircam.py. Provenance lives
# in info/provenance/*.json. B1938+666 alone is ~80 GB of uncal, so none of it enters git history.
#
# data/stamps is the deliberate exception (as in the HST repo): the final science stamps
# are small and carry the hand-drawn, non-regenerable masks and positions. Every stamp size
# shares a band dir and is named by its size (scripts/stamp_paths.py); only each lens's
# MODELLING size is tracked -- 12" by default, 7" for B1938+666 (its stamp_size in
# info/samples/lens_samples.json). A lens given a new stamp_size needs its own
# !data/stamps/**/stamp<S>_* line here, or its stamps are silently ignored.
data/*
!data/stamps/
!data/qc/
data/stamps/**/stamp*
!data/stamps/**/stamp12_*
!data/stamps/**/stamp7_*
# QC renders, as in the HST repo (2026-10-04): stamp<S>_positions.png is a view OF the tracked
# positions JSON (rebuilt by make_positions.py --overlays-only), and stamp<S>.png a plain
# render of the tracked sci stamp (rebuilt by make_stamps.py). Neither is a product, and every
# re-cut adds a ~0.5-1.2 MB version to history. Both are already excluded by the stamp*
# rule above (the bare render has no underscore after the size, the overlay is re-ignored
# here); stamp<S>_dataset.png stays tracked.
data/stamps/**/*_positions.png

# ── Generated / local ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
output/
diagnostics/
/local/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.venv/
# CRDS cache and STPSF data live under data/ (ignored above) -- see AGENTS.md, Environment.

# personal shell setup (venv activation, host aliases); not needed to use the repo
activate_local.sh

# ── Machine-local records ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# export_dataset.py logs each export keyed by its absolute --dest path, which only means
# something on the machine that ran it.
info/provenance/lens_exports.json

# ── Private agent notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md imports the tracked AGENTS.md (@AGENTS.md) and adds the maintainer's private
# working notes. Only AGENTS.md is needed to use the repo.
/CLAUDE.md
